 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Reprojection Bounds:** If $p'$ falls outside the image boundaries of the target view, the consistency check cannot be performed. The method marks these as invalid (0) [S1, unofficial].
-- **Occlusions:** Multi-view consistency may fail at occlusion boundaries where the NeRF depth and MDE depth disagree due to different geometric interpretations. The threshold $\tau$ must be tuned to handle these discrepancies [S1, unofficial].
-- **NeRF Accuracy:** The method relies on the NeRF depth $\bar{D}_l$ being reasonably accurate. If the NeRF is poorly trained, the confidence mask may incorrectly filter valid MDE depth or retain invalid depth [S1, unofficial].
